{"id":"mahabharata-12-054","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":54,"title":"चतुःपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 54 · Bhishma agrees to teach","summary":{"en":"Janamejaya asks how Bhishma, pained by his wounds, could teach, and Vaishampayana tells how Yudhishthira begs him and Krishna speaks. Bhishma, relieved of pain by Krishna's grace, agrees to teach all the ancient dharmas.","kn":"ಗಾಯದ ನೋವಿನಿಂದ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಬೋಧಿಸುವುದು ಹೇಗೆಂದು ಜನಮೇಜಯ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಬೇಡಿ ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಮಾತನಾಡಿದುದನ್ನು ವೈಶಂಪಾಯನ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕೃಷ್ಣನ ಕೃಪೆಯಿಂದ ನೋವು ಮುಕ್ತನಾದ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಸನಾತನ ಧರ್ಮಗಳನ್ನು ಬೋಧಿಸಲು ಒಪ್ಪುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"जनमेजय पूछते हैं कि घावों से पीड़ित भीष्म ने कैसे उपदेश दिया, और वैशम्पायन बताते हैं कि युधिष्ठिर ने विनती की और कृष्ण ने कहा। कृष्ण की कृपा से पीड़ामुक्त भीष्म सब सनातन धर्म सिखाने को मान जाते हैं।","te":"గాయాల నొప్పితో భీష్ముడు ఎలా బోధించాడని జనమేజయుడు అడుగుతాడు; యుధిష్ఠిరుడు ప్రార్థించి కృష్ణుడు మాట్లాడిన తీరును వైశంపాయనుడు చెబుతాడు. కృష్ణుని కృపతో నొప్పి తొలగిన భీష్ముడు సనాతన ధర్మాలను బోధించడానికి అంగీకరిస్తాడు.","ta":"காயங்களின் வலியுடன் பீஷ்மர் எவ்வாறு போதித்தார் என்று ஜனமேஜயன் கேட்க, யுதிஷ்டிரர் வேண்டியதையும் கண்ணன் பேசியதையும் வைசம்பாயனர் கூறுகிறார். கண்ணனின் அருளால் வலி நீங்கிய பீஷ்மர் பழம் தர்மங்களைக் கற்பிக்க ஒப்புகிறார்.","ml":"മുറിവുകളുടെ വേദനയോടെ ഭീഷ്മർ എങ്ങനെ പഠിപ്പിച്ചുവെന്ന് ജനമേജയൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നതും കൃഷ്ണൻ സംസാരിക്കുന്നതും വൈശമ്പായനൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു. കൃഷ്ണന്റെ കൃപയാൽ വേദന ശമിച്ച ഭീഷ്മർ പുരാതന ധർമ്മങ്ങളെല്ലാം പഠിപ്പിക്കാൻ സമ്മതിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.54; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"धर्मात्मनि महासत्त्वे सत्यसंधे जितात्मनि ।\nदेवव्रते महाभागे शरतल्पगतेऽच्युते ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the righteous-souled, mighty, truthful, self-mastered and blessed Devavrata, the unfallen one, lay on his bed of arrows,"}},{"n":2,"text":"शयाने वीरशयने भीष्मे शंतनुनन्दने ।\nगाङ्गेये पुरुषव्याघ्रे पाण्डवैः पर्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"when Bhishma, delight of Shantanu and tiger among men, Ganga's son, lay on his hero's bed and the Pandavas stood by him,"}},{"n":3,"text":"काः कथाः समवर्तन्त तस्मिन्वीरसमागमे ।\nहतेषु सर्वसैन्येषु तन्मे शंस महामुने ॥","meaning":{"en":"what talk took place at that meeting of heroes after all the armies had been slain? Tell me this, great sage."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"शरतल्पगते भीष्मे कौरवाणां धुरंधरे ।\nआजग्मुरृषयः सिद्धा नारदप्रमुखा नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Bhishma, bearer of the Kuru burden, lay on his bed of arrows, sages and siddhas headed by Narada came, king."}},{"n":5,"text":"हतशिष्टाश्च राजानो युधिष्ठिरपुरोगमाः ।\nधृतराष्ट्रश्च कृष्णश्च भीमार्जुनयमास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"So did the kings who survived the slaughter, led by Yudhishthira, and Dhritarashtra, Krishna, Bhima, Arjuna and the twins."}},{"n":6,"text":"तेऽभिगम्य महात्मानो भरतानां पितामहम् ।\nअन्वशोचन्त गाङ्गेयमादित्यं पतितं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Approaching the grandfather of the Bharatas, those great souls grieved for Ganga's son as for a sun fallen from the sky."}},{"n":7,"text":"मुहूर्तमिव च ध्यात्वा नारदो देवदर्शनः ।\nउवाच पाण्डवान्सर्वान्हतशिष्टांश्च पार्थिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"After meditating for a moment, Narada, who sees the gods, spoke to all the Pandavas and the surviving kings."}},{"n":8,"text":"प्राप्तकालं च आचक्षे भीष्मोऽयमनुयुज्यताम् ।\nअस्तमेति हि गाङ्गेयो भानुमानिव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The time has come, I tell you; let Bhishma now be questioned. Ganga's son is setting like the sun, descendant of Bharata."}},{"n":9,"text":"अयं प्राणानुत्सिसृक्षुस्तं सर्वेऽभ्येत्य पृच्छत ।\nकृत्स्नान्हि विविधान्धर्मांश्चातुर्वर्ण्यस्य वेत्त्ययम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He wishes to give up his life, so all of you approach and ask him; he knows all the various duties of the four classes in full."}},{"n":10,"text":"एष वृद्धः पुरा लोकान्संप्राप्नोति तनुत्यजाम् ।\nतं शीघ्रमनुयुञ्जध्वं संशयान्मनसि स्थितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This elder will soon reach the worlds of those who lay down the body; question him quickly about the doubts in your minds."}},{"n":11,"text":"एवमुक्ता नारदेन भीष्ममीयुर्नराधिपाः ।\nप्रष्टुं चाशक्नुवन्तस्ते वीक्षां चक्रुः परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by Narada, the kings went to Bhishma, but unable to ask, they looked at one another."}},{"n":12,"text":"अथोवाच हृषीकेशं पाण्डुपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nनान्यस्त्वद्देवकीपुत्र शक्तः प्रष्टुं पितामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira, son of Pandu, said to Hrishikesha: No one but you, son of Devaki, is able to question the grandfather."}},{"n":13,"text":"प्रव्याहारय दुर्धर्ष त्वमग्रे मधुसूदन ।\nत्वं हि नस्तात सर्वेषां सर्वधर्मविदुत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Invincible Madhusudana, you speak to him first; you, dear one, are the best knower of all dharma among us all."}},{"n":14,"text":"एवमुक्तः पाण्डवेन भगवान्केशवस्तदा ।\nअभिगम्य दुराधर्षं प्रव्याहारयदच्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by the Pandava, the blessed unfallen Keshava went up to the unassailable Bhishma and spoke."}},{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"कच्चित्सुखेन रजनी व्युष्टा ते राजसत्तम ।\nविस्पष्टलक्षणा बुद्धिः कच्चिच्चोपस्थिता तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of kings, has the night passed easily for you? Is your mind clear and its marks distinct and ready?"}},{"n":16,"text":"कच्चिज्ज्ञानानि सर्वाणि प्रतिभान्ति च तेऽनघ ।\nन ग्लायते च हृदयं न च ते व्याकुलं मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Blameless one, do all your branches of knowledge come to you? Is your heart not sinking, nor your mind disturbed?"}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"दाहो मोहः श्रमश्चैव क्लमो ग्लानिस्तथा रुजा ।\nतव प्रसादाद्गोविन्द सद्यो व्यपगतानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Burning, confusion, weariness, exhaustion, faintness and pain have all left me at once by your grace, Govinda, blameless one."}},{"n":18,"text":"यच्च भूतं भविष्यच्च भवच्च परमद्युते ।\nतत्सर्वमनुपश्यामि पाणौ फलमिवाहितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All that has been, will be and is, radiant one, I see as clearly as a fruit set in the palm of the hand."}},{"n":19,"text":"वेदोक्ताश्चैव ये धर्मा वेदान्तनिहिताश्च ये ।\nतान्सर्वान्संप्रपश्यामि वरदानात्तवाच्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever duties are declared in the Vedas and set down in the Vedanta I see completely, Achyuta, through your boon."}},{"n":20,"text":"शिष्टैश्च धर्मो यः प्रोक्तः स च मे हृदि वर्तते ।\nदेशजातिकुलानां च धर्मज्ञोऽस्मि जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"The dharma that the learned have declared lives in my heart, and I know the dharma of lands, castes and families, Janardana."}},{"n":21,"text":"चतुर्ष्वाश्रमधर्मेषु योऽर्थः स च हृदि स्थितः ।\nराजधर्मांश्च सकलानवगच्छामि केशव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever the purpose is in the duties of the four stages of life is fixed in my heart, and I understand all the duties of kings, Keshava."}},{"n":22,"text":"यत्र यत्र च वक्तव्यं तद्वक्ष्यामि जनार्दन ।\nतव प्रसादाद्धि शुभा मनो मे बुद्धिराविशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wherever something must be said, I shall say it, Janardana; by your grace a good understanding has entered my mind."}},{"n":23,"text":"युवेव चास्मि संवृत्तस्त्वदनुध्यानबृंहितः ।\nवक्तुं श्रेयः समर्थोऽस्मि त्वत्प्रसादाज्जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Strengthened by your meditation I have become as if young again, and by your grace I am able to speak of what is best, Janardana."}},{"n":24,"text":"स्वयं किमर्थं तु भवाञ्श्रेयो न प्राह पाण्डवम् ।\nकिं ते विवक्षितं चात्र तदाशु वद माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"But why did you not tell the Pandava what is best yourself? What did you wish to say here? Tell me at once, Madhava."}},{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"यशसः श्रेयसश्चैव मूलं मां विद्धि कौरव ।\nमत्तः सर्वेऽभिनिर्वृत्ता भावाः सदसदात्मकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know me, Kaurava, as the root of fame and of the highest good; all things, real and unreal in nature, have come out of me."}},{"n":26,"text":"शीतांशुश्चन्द्र इत्युक्ते को लोके विस्मयिष्यति ।\nतथैव यशसा पूर्णे मयि को विस्मयिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the cool-rayed moon is called the moon, who in the world will wonder? Likewise who will wonder at me, full of fame?"}},{"n":27,"text":"आधेयं तु मया भूयो यशस्तव महाद्युते ।\nततो मे विपुला बुद्धिस्त्वयि भीष्म समाहिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"But, greatly radiant one, I wish to place still more fame on you; therefore my great intent is set on you, Bhishma."}},{"n":28,"text":"यावद्धि पृथिवीपाल पृथिवी स्थास्यते ध्रुवा ।\nतावत्तवाक्षया कीर्तिर्लोकाननु चरिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"As long as the earth, protector of the earth, stands firm, so long your undying fame will travel through the worlds."}},{"n":29,"text":"यच्च त्वं वक्ष्यसे भीष्म पाण्डवायानुपृच्छते ।\nवेदप्रवादा इव ते स्थास्यन्ति वसुधातले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever you tell the Pandava as he questions you, Bhishma, will remain on the face of the earth like the word of the Veda."}},{"n":30,"text":"यश्चैतेन प्रमाणेन योक्ष्यत्यात्मानमात्मना ।\nस फलं सर्वपुण्यानां प्रेत्य चानुभविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever joins himself by himself to this authority will enjoy the fruit of all meritorious acts after death."}},{"n":31,"text":"एतस्मात्कारणाद्भीष्म मतिर्दिव्या मया हि ते ।\nदत्ता यशो विप्रथेत कथं भूयस्तवेति ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"For this reason, Bhishma, I gave you this divine insight, so that your fame may spread still further."}},{"n":32,"text":"यावद्धि प्रथते लोके पुरुषस्य यशो भुवि ।\nतावत्तस्याक्षयं स्थानं भवतीति विनिश्चितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As long as a man's fame spreads in the world on earth, so long, it is certain, his place is undying."}},{"n":33,"text":"राजानो हतशिष्टास्त्वां राजन्नभित आसते ।\nधर्माननुयुयुक्षन्तस्तेभ्यः प्रब्रूहि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The surviving kings sit around you, king, wishing to ask about dharma; speak to them, descendant of Bharata."}},{"n":34,"text":"भवान्हि वयसा वृद्धः श्रुताचारसमन्वितः ।\nकुशलो राजधर्माणां पूर्वेषामपराश्च ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are advanced in years, endowed with learning and conduct, and skilled in the duties of kings, of earlier times and later."}},{"n":35,"text":"जन्मप्रभृति ते कश्चिद्वृजिनं न ददर्श ह ।\nज्ञातारमनुधर्माणां त्वां विदुः सर्वपार्थिवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From birth no one has seen any wrong in you, and all kings know you as the knower of the dharma that follows tradition."}},{"n":36,"text":"तेभ्यः पितेव पुत्रेभ्यो राजन्ब्रूहि परं नयम् ।\nऋषयश्च हि देवाश्च त्वया नित्यमुपासिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, king, as a father to his sons, tell them the highest policy; sages and gods have always been served by you."}},{"n":37,"text":"तस्माद्वक्तव्यमेवेह त्वया पश्याम्यशेषतः ।\nधर्माञ्शुश्रूषमाणेभ्यः पृष्टेन च सता पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore you must speak here, and I see this fully: a good man who is questioned by those eager to hear of dharma must answer."}},{"n":38,"text":"वक्तव्यं विदुषा चेति धर्ममाहुर्मनीषिणः ।\nअप्रतिब्रुवतः कष्टो दोषो हि भवति प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise say that dharma is that a learned man must speak when asked; for one who does not reply, lord, there is a painful fault."}},{"n":39,"text":"तस्मात्पुत्रैश्च पौत्रैश्च धर्मान्पृष्टः सनातनान् ।\nविद्वाञ्जिज्ञासमानैस्त्वं प्रब्रूहि भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, bull of the Bharatas, being asked about eternal dharma by sons and grandsons who wish to know, you should answer."}}]}]}